Error [E0956]: `LEXED` holds a compiler value (`CompilerLexed`), which exists only while compiling
  --> compiler_value_read_at_runtime_is_rejected_2.jet:8:11
    |
  8 |     print(LEXED.tokens.len())
    |           ^^^^^
 Why: Comptime code and `fn build` read compiler values; the running program has no compiler to answer them
 Fix: Compute the plain value you need (a Bool, number or String) inside a `comptime` block and read that at runtime
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0956
